WEBVTT

00:00:34.785 --> 00:00:37.527
Mom on deck! Ten... Ho!

00:00:37.788 --> 00:00:41.451
All right, grunts, here's
your pre-mission pep talk.

00:00:41.667 --> 00:00:43.908
Shoot anyone
who doesn't obey hard enough.

00:00:44.711 --> 00:00:45.791
But...

00:00:47.506 --> 00:00:49.087
Stop gaining knowledge,
Hubert.

00:00:50.509 --> 00:00:51.874
Lt's a simple mission.

00:00:51.969 --> 00:00:54.381
The grunts catch the alien,
the surgeon guts it,

00:00:54.471 --> 00:00:56.462
and you smuggle the
poison parts back here.

00:00:56.557 --> 00:00:59.173
Uh, something
about poison, got it.

00:00:59.268 --> 00:01:02.180
By the way,
that surgeon, where is he?

00:01:02.271 --> 00:01:03.636
You! Where's the butcher?

00:01:03.730 --> 00:01:05.516
Ma'am, I don't know, ma'am.
His duffel bag arrlved.

00:01:06.900 --> 00:01:09.141
Lt's not a duffel bag.
It's my apartment!

00:01:11.113 --> 00:01:12.819
Hubert, meet John Zoidberg.

00:01:12.906 --> 00:01:16.398
You need an alien hacked to
pieces, he's the best there is,

00:01:16.593 --> 00:01:17.753
in the budget category.

00:01:17.844 --> 00:01:20.256
Have you ever
dissected a Yeti before?

00:01:21.056 --> 00:01:22.171
Himalayan or Neptunian?

00:01:22.307 --> 00:01:23.422
Tritonian.

00:01:23.600 --> 00:01:26.137
A Tritonian Yeti?

00:01:26.228 --> 00:01:28.685
You two aren't up to
anything unethical, are you?

00:01:28.772 --> 00:01:29.978
Relax.

00:01:30.065 --> 00:01:33.774
There's nothing unethical about
covert biological weapons research.

00:01:34.152 --> 00:01:35.141
I said, "Relax!"

00:01:35.237 --> 00:01:36.226
Ooh!
Ooh!

00:01:40.242 --> 00:01:44.201
Ah, Zoidberg, we've known each
other so long that sometimes

00:01:44.287 --> 00:01:47.825
I don't think we even need
words to understand each other.

00:01:47.916 --> 00:01:48.905
What?

00:01:52.921 --> 00:01:54.252
Once and for all, Fry,

00:01:54.339 --> 00:01:57.831
even though it's the future, most
objects are still just objects,

00:01:57.968 --> 00:02:00.175
not aliens who
look like objects.

00:02:00.303 --> 00:02:02.715
So my efforts to establish
diplomatic relations

00:02:02.806 --> 00:02:05.172
with the Cactus People
were doomed from the start.

00:02:07.894 --> 00:02:10.727
So you're in pain and
have a bunch of needles?

00:02:10.814 --> 00:02:13.305
I prescribe acupuncture.
Let's begin.

00:02:14.985 --> 00:02:15.974
Blood?

00:02:16.069 --> 00:02:17.775
I mean, blood.

00:02:17.863 --> 00:02:18.978
Put it back in me!

00:02:20.615 --> 00:02:23.152
I'm afraid Fry
lost a lot of juice.

00:02:23.285 --> 00:02:25.401
He's developed
Simpsons Jaundice.

00:02:25.495 --> 00:02:26.610
Ay, caramba!

00:02:26.705 --> 00:02:28.866
His only hope is
some replacement liver.

00:02:28.957 --> 00:02:30.948
Yours looks like
a good match.

00:02:31.126 --> 00:02:33.117
Well, if it'll help Fry...

00:02:33.211 --> 00:02:36.203
Careful, Leela! He knows less
about human anatomy than I do.

00:02:36.339 --> 00:02:38.421
And I can't even
find my own uterus.

00:02:39.176 --> 00:02:41.792
You may feel
a slight sawing.

00:02:43.346 --> 00:02:45.883
And all we need is
a little spine supplement

00:02:45.974 --> 00:02:49.341
to replace what Leela lost in
that unavoidable saw mix-up.

00:02:49.519 --> 00:02:51.350
It wasn't unavoidable.

00:02:51.438 --> 00:02:53.929
You just had to stop cutting
my spine when I yelled,

00:02:54.024 --> 00:02:56.390
"Stop, you're cutting
my spine!"

00:02:56.485 --> 00:02:57.895
Quit complaining!

00:02:58.278 --> 00:03:02.021
My body rejected your liver, and
now I've got Garfield Syndrome.

00:03:02.115 --> 00:03:03.901
Oh, I hate Mondays.

00:03:03.992 --> 00:03:07.450
Anyhow, Hermes, all Leela
needs is one of your vertebrae.

00:03:07.537 --> 00:03:10.495
But, Doctor, will I be
able to limbo afterwards?

00:03:10.582 --> 00:03:12.197
Could you limbo before?

00:03:14.127 --> 00:03:18.291
Wait. I say, "Yes," and you
say, "I couldn't limbo before."

00:03:18.423 --> 00:03:19.959
You ruined the joke,
Hermes.

00:03:21.843 --> 00:03:24.129
There you go, Leela.
Good as new!

00:03:24.221 --> 00:03:26.553
Whoa! Whoa!

00:03:26.723 --> 00:03:28.463
Oh. Sure,
Leela's fine,

00:03:28.558 --> 00:03:31.265
but my jaundice has
progressed to Muppet Gangrene!

00:03:31.353 --> 00:03:33.093
Lt's not easy
being gangrenous.

00:03:33.980 --> 00:03:36.517
I thought you were only gonna
take out one vertebra!

00:03:36.608 --> 00:03:38.815
Yeah, but did you ever
play Jenga?

00:03:38.902 --> 00:03:40.642
Sometimes you pull one and...

00:03:41.613 --> 00:03:43.478
Yeah, well, I'm not staying like this.

00:03:43.573 --> 00:03:45.063
I can't believe it.

00:03:45.742 --> 00:03:49.655
Mmm. What started out as a pleasant
afternoon of drugs and surgery

00:03:49.746 --> 00:03:51.282
has not gone as planned.

00:03:51.373 --> 00:03:52.328
But don't worry,

00:03:52.415 --> 00:03:56.283
we still have three or four
co-workers with plenty of spare parts.

00:03:59.089 --> 00:04:01.296
My first mission.
I'm so excited.

00:04:01.424 --> 00:04:03.790
And after I dissect
the Yeti's poison glands,

00:04:03.885 --> 00:04:06.342
we can stop, maybe, for
ice cream on the way back?

00:04:06.429 --> 00:04:07.589
With sprinkles on?

00:04:07.848 --> 00:04:12.638
Why, you're just a big
kid, aren't you, Zoidberg?

00:04:12.727 --> 00:04:14.183
A very big kid!

00:04:14.271 --> 00:04:16.227
We're over the drop zone, gentlemen.

00:04:16.314 --> 00:04:19.431
Might I suggest you jump out
the door and poop yourselves?

00:04:24.489 --> 00:04:26.445
Aah!

00:04:27.784 --> 00:04:31.447
So anyway, I hope the men have been
taking their hyper-malaria pills.

00:04:31.538 --> 00:04:32.823
Their what?

00:04:32.956 --> 00:04:35.698
"Their what?"

00:04:35.792 --> 00:04:38.078
That's funny,
like a crazy old man.

00:04:38.169 --> 00:04:39.750
But you know
what's not funny?

00:04:39.838 --> 00:04:42.170
Deadly Tritonian
hyper-malaria.

00:04:42.299 --> 00:04:44.540
Just be sure to stay out
of the methane swamps.

00:04:48.805 --> 00:04:50.136
What smells like methane?

00:04:54.811 --> 00:04:57.518
My God! I've never seen
such a gruesome shark attack.

00:04:57.606 --> 00:04:59.062
Especially
this far inland.

00:04:59.149 --> 00:05:02.562
It wasn't a shark. It was
an awful, incompetent doctor.

00:05:02.652 --> 00:05:04.608
Wow, he must've been
a total Zoidberg.

00:05:04.696 --> 00:05:06.277
It was Zoidberg!

00:05:06.364 --> 00:05:10.403
He brutalized us with power
tools, gypsy curses and hypnosis.

00:05:10.493 --> 00:05:12.529
Yes, master.

00:05:12.621 --> 00:05:15.488
You'll all get through this. I
give you my word as a real doctor.

00:05:15.582 --> 00:05:16.742
What about me?

00:05:16.833 --> 00:05:17.822
What did he do to you?

00:05:17.918 --> 00:05:21.160
I don't know exactly,
but I'm incontinent.

00:05:21.546 --> 00:05:23.127
I'm truly sorry.

00:05:23.506 --> 00:05:25.747
I consider myself
a reasonable man.

00:05:25.842 --> 00:05:27.924
Quick with a joke,
slow to anger.

00:05:28.011 --> 00:05:30.172
But Bender can't go on
long car trips anymore,

00:05:30.263 --> 00:05:32.049
and I say Zoidberg must die.

00:05:32.140 --> 00:05:34.426
People, please.
Let's not overreact...

00:05:35.894 --> 00:05:37.509
Death to the crab!

00:05:44.486 --> 00:05:45.976
How bad is it,
Doctor?

00:05:46.071 --> 00:05:48.938
Super bad. It's
Tritonian hyper-malaria.

00:05:49.032 --> 00:05:52.024
A lot of these men will
be dead within 24 hours.

00:05:52.118 --> 00:05:53.949
What?
Not you, though.

00:05:54.037 --> 00:05:55.777
You'll make
a complete recovery

00:05:55.914 --> 00:05:57.654
and go on to
marry a supermodel!

00:05:59.209 --> 00:06:01.200
Funny plague,
hyper-malaria.

00:06:01.294 --> 00:06:04.536
It can kill immediately,
or lie dormant for decades.

00:06:04.631 --> 00:06:06.747
But sooner or later,
it erupts,

00:06:06.841 --> 00:06:11.801
causing fever, spasms, madness,
coma, and finally death.

00:06:11.888 --> 00:06:12.923
What?

00:06:13.014 --> 00:06:14.094
Supermodel!

00:06:14.182 --> 00:06:17.925
Oh! Those poor,
doomed bastards.

00:06:18.269 --> 00:06:20.976
I guess it's up to me
to complete the mission.

00:06:25.110 --> 00:06:29.319
I'll be in the swamp, blowing
the smirk off a toxic Yeti.

00:06:36.329 --> 00:06:39.446
Professor, we need
to talk, man-to-mob.

00:06:41.793 --> 00:06:45.126
We've had it with Zoidberg!
We demand you fire him!

00:06:45.255 --> 00:06:49.373
Nonsense. Zoidberg's a
fine physician, for aliens.

00:06:49.467 --> 00:06:51.458
Your mistake
is being humans.

00:06:51.553 --> 00:06:55.171
No, if I'm going to fire
anyone, it'll be Scruffy.

00:06:55.265 --> 00:06:56.505
You can't do that.

00:06:56.599 --> 00:06:58.089
Over my dead body!

00:06:58.476 --> 00:07:00.182
Don't you get it,
old man?

00:07:00.270 --> 00:07:04.104
Thanks to Dr. Scissorhands, I
wet myself every time I laugh.

00:07:05.400 --> 00:07:06.731
Lt's not funny!

00:07:06.818 --> 00:07:09.230
Well, I guess it is
kind of funny.

00:07:09.320 --> 00:07:10.355
Oh-oh.

00:07:10.447 --> 00:07:12.563
Why are you protecting
Zoidberg, Professor?

00:07:12.657 --> 00:07:13.817
Do you owe him
something?

00:07:13.950 --> 00:07:15.690
Is he blackmailing you somehow?

00:07:15.785 --> 00:07:17.525
What does he have
on you?

00:07:17.620 --> 00:07:19.406
Why have you kept him around
all these years

00:07:19.497 --> 00:07:21.658
when he's so grossly
incompetent?

00:07:23.626 --> 00:07:28.290
Long ago, Zoidberg and I
entered into a secret arrangement

00:07:28.381 --> 00:07:33.125
relating to certain extraordinary
events too horrible to reveal.

00:07:33.219 --> 00:07:36.461
So there's nothing
to be curious about.

00:07:47.650 --> 00:07:48.639
Oh!

00:07:48.735 --> 00:07:51.226
Stop, or I'll shoot!

00:07:52.489 --> 00:07:53.478
Zoidberg?

00:07:53.823 --> 00:07:56.906
You can't hunt a Yeti by
yourself, sir. It's suicidal!

00:07:56.993 --> 00:08:00.736
So what? I'm going to die
of hyper-malaria, anyway.

00:08:00.830 --> 00:08:03.572
I was in the same swamp
as the rest of the men.

00:08:03.666 --> 00:08:06.282
Just because you were in the
swamp doesn't necessarily mean...

00:08:06.377 --> 00:08:10.290
I was thirsty from the
flight. I drank swamp water.

00:08:10.381 --> 00:08:13.498
Look, Zoidberg,
you're a loyal friend.

00:08:14.135 --> 00:08:14.796
"Friend"?

00:08:14.821 --> 00:08:16.167
But I'm doomed!

00:08:16.262 --> 00:08:19.504
I might as well capture a Yeti
and die trying.

00:08:20.183 --> 00:08:23.641
Then you'll need someone
to dissect it, friend.

00:08:27.982 --> 00:08:30.143
Go, Johnny! Go!
That's an order!

00:08:30.235 --> 00:08:33.398
Never! Zoidberg doesn't
abandon a friend, apparently.

00:08:42.205 --> 00:08:45.948
I'll save us by scaring him
off with my crazy war noise.

00:08:51.881 --> 00:08:54.918
Crunch all you want.
I'll make more.

00:08:57.887 --> 00:09:00.378
Oy. I lost another one.

00:09:01.391 --> 00:09:04.053
Zoidberg, I'm sorry to
break it to you this way,

00:09:04.144 --> 00:09:06.635
but we hate you and we
never wanna see you again.

00:09:06.729 --> 00:09:08.139
But, friends...

00:09:08.231 --> 00:09:10.893
We're not your friends!
We're your victims!

00:09:10.984 --> 00:09:12.099
I was just
trying to...

00:09:12.193 --> 00:09:13.933
Shut up and give me
my kidney back!

00:09:15.238 --> 00:09:16.478
I'm sorry.

00:09:17.198 --> 00:09:18.563
I'm sorry.

00:09:19.409 --> 00:09:21.320
We don't know why the
Professor keeps you around here,

00:09:21.411 --> 00:09:22.617
and we don't care.

00:09:22.704 --> 00:09:24.069
You're a terrible doctor!

00:09:24.164 --> 00:09:26.325
Nobody wants to
see you ever again!

00:09:26.416 --> 00:09:29.453
Dr. Zoidberg! I want
to see you right now!

00:09:35.258 --> 00:09:37.374
The time
has come, my friend.

00:09:37.468 --> 00:09:40.585
We have to talk
about our arrangement.

00:09:40.722 --> 00:09:45.386
Oh, no. No, no.
Oh, no, no, no! Oh, no!

00:09:45.476 --> 00:09:46.966
Oh, no!

00:09:49.063 --> 00:09:51.475
Un-paw him,
you big ape!

00:09:51.941 --> 00:09:53.852
I saw this in a Tarzan movie!

00:09:54.235 --> 00:09:57.944
Lt was called
Tarzan versus the Yetis.

00:09:58.656 --> 00:10:01.523
I lost my virginity
during the film,

00:10:01.659 --> 00:10:04.526
so I'm a little fuzzy
on the details.

00:10:06.289 --> 00:10:07.699
Oh!

00:10:19.135 --> 00:10:20.796
John, are you all right?

00:10:21.179 --> 00:10:23.420
You...
You saved my life!

00:10:23.765 --> 00:10:24.720
Oh, fuff.

00:10:24.807 --> 00:10:25.796
Yes, fuff.

00:10:25.892 --> 00:10:27.678
How can I ever
repay you?

00:10:27.769 --> 00:10:30.181
Do you need a slave?
Or maybe a butler?

00:10:30.271 --> 00:10:33.638
No, I haven't needed a butler
since grad school.

00:10:33.733 --> 00:10:35.223
But I do need a doctor.

00:10:35.735 --> 00:10:38.477
I don't want to die
like those Marines, John.

00:10:38.571 --> 00:10:40.778
The fever, the madness.

00:10:40.865 --> 00:10:43.231
Don't forget the spasms,
coma and death.

00:10:43.409 --> 00:10:47.652
Oh. I don't want to go through
that. I want you to kill me.

00:10:47.747 --> 00:10:49.112
All right.
Give me the knife.

00:10:49.207 --> 00:10:53.325
Not now! Hyper-malaria
can lie dormant for years.

00:10:53.419 --> 00:10:54.829
Isn't that what you said?

00:10:54.921 --> 00:10:57.003
Lt sounds like
something I would say.

00:10:57.090 --> 00:11:00.127
So stay with me
until the symptoms start,

00:11:00.260 --> 00:11:02.626
then put me
out of my misery.

00:11:02.720 --> 00:11:04.005
You must swear!

00:11:06.516 --> 00:11:09.474
All right, Hubert,
I swear.

00:11:12.230 --> 00:11:16.644
It's started, Zoidberg, the
fever, the muscle spasms.

00:11:17.527 --> 00:11:18.516
I'm dying.

00:11:20.113 --> 00:11:23.697
Lt's time for you to keep
your promise and kill me.

00:11:23.783 --> 00:11:28.402
This is very difficult,
but I'll try, friend.

00:11:36.587 --> 00:11:38.873
No, wait,
I'm afraid to die.

00:11:39.090 --> 00:11:41.456
Ah. You said
you wanted me to kill you.

00:11:41.551 --> 00:11:43.963
Is this one of those
"no means yes" deals?

00:11:44.053 --> 00:11:45.463
Yes and no.

00:11:45.555 --> 00:11:48.888
I do want you to kill me,
but I mustn't see it coming.

00:11:48.975 --> 00:11:50.055
That would be agony.

00:11:50.393 --> 00:11:53.556
So you must murder me
completely by surprise.

00:11:53.938 --> 00:11:57.055
As God is my witness,
you can count on me.

00:11:57.734 --> 00:11:59.850
Well, see you tomorrow.

00:12:05.408 --> 00:12:07.023
Not surprising enough.

00:12:31.434 --> 00:12:32.799
Oh. Ah!

00:12:32.894 --> 00:12:35.306
My heart!

00:12:42.945 --> 00:12:43.934
Ho.

00:12:52.789 --> 00:12:54.120
Hey.
What are you doing there?

00:12:54.207 --> 00:12:58.075
Whoa, whoa, whoa, whoa.

00:12:58.169 --> 00:12:59.830
Stop, you don't
understand.

00:12:59.921 --> 00:13:02.958
Let's go, you murderer.
Fry, help me lock him up.

00:13:03.049 --> 00:13:05.256
Hang on. I'm learning
how to do loop-de-loops.

00:13:05.343 --> 00:13:06.958
Whoa, whoa!

00:13:08.763 --> 00:13:13.257
You're making a mistake. I was
only trying to kill the Professor.

00:13:21.818 --> 00:13:23.979
Hubert, I'm sorry.

00:13:25.822 --> 00:13:27.687
Huh? He doesn't have hair.

00:13:29.033 --> 00:13:30.944
Great Little Caesar's ghost!

00:13:31.035 --> 00:13:35.574
You fools, you stupid,
life-prolonging fools.

00:13:35.665 --> 00:13:38.498
I asked Zoidberg
to kill me.

00:13:38.626 --> 00:13:39.706
What you talking about, Professor? What?

00:13:39.794 --> 00:13:41.330
Professor, have you gone mad?

00:13:41.421 --> 00:13:45.664
Probably. It's one of the symptoms
of Tritonian hyper-malaria.

00:13:45.800 --> 00:13:49.292
You mean the incurable
disease that causes fever,

00:13:49.470 --> 00:13:51.426
spasms, insanity,

00:13:51.514 --> 00:13:53.095
Coma,

00:13:54.350 --> 00:13:55.339
And finally death?

00:13:56.936 --> 00:14:00.929
Yes, and I begged Zoidberg
to put me out of my misery.

00:14:01.399 --> 00:14:03.310
Bring him, quickly.

00:14:08.156 --> 00:14:11.273
Should have known better than to
store my antiques in the office.

00:14:11.367 --> 00:14:13.278
Zoidberg,
we were wrong.

00:14:13.369 --> 00:14:16.577
We're letting you out so
you can kill the Professor.

00:14:20.001 --> 00:14:22.413
No, he sand-crabbed out.

00:14:22.670 --> 00:14:24.831
Then we
have no choice.

00:14:24.922 --> 00:14:27.334
We'll have to mercy-kill
the Professor ourselves.

00:14:27.425 --> 00:14:29.416
Well, let's get started.

00:14:34.765 --> 00:14:36.380
We have a situation, Mother.

00:14:36.476 --> 00:14:39.183
This creature tried to
sand-crab into the building.

00:14:39.270 --> 00:14:40.601
Zoidberg?

00:14:40.688 --> 00:14:43.521
Sorry I didn't call first,
Carol, but I'm in a hurry.

00:14:43.608 --> 00:14:45.189
I need your help
to save Hubert.

00:14:45.276 --> 00:14:47.688
Let him go and stooge
the hell out of here.

00:14:47.778 --> 00:14:48.767
We're on it.

00:14:51.073 --> 00:14:54.110
Beautiful kids.
You must be very proud.

00:14:54.202 --> 00:14:58.616
John Zoidberg. It's been a
long time. How have you been?

00:14:58.706 --> 00:14:59.866
Not too bad.

00:14:59.957 --> 00:15:02.539
Last year I took a bus trip
to the Grand Canyon.

00:15:02.627 --> 00:15:04.208
Later, I'll show you
the pictures.

00:15:04.295 --> 00:15:07.879
Do you ever regret it, John,
leaving me to work for the Professor?

00:15:08.090 --> 00:15:09.079
Oh...

00:15:09.175 --> 00:15:12.338
What do you want me to say?
He saved my life.

00:15:12.428 --> 00:15:15.465
Big deal. You could have
been rich if you'd stayed.

00:15:15.556 --> 00:15:17.842
Your own lab,
a full staff.

00:15:17.934 --> 00:15:20.095
But Hubert is my friend.

00:15:20.186 --> 00:15:21.676
He's very sick.

00:15:21.771 --> 00:15:26.686
I can cure him, but I need the
thing, the thing from Triton.

00:15:26.776 --> 00:15:30.018
It'll cost you, John.
How much are you worth now?

00:15:30.112 --> 00:15:31.818
I live in a dumpster.

00:15:31.906 --> 00:15:34.113
All I have in the world
is this coupon

00:15:34.200 --> 00:15:36.361
for one free session
at the tanning salon.

00:15:36.619 --> 00:15:40.282
Oh, John, that's really all you have?

00:15:42.542 --> 00:15:44.999
Then, I'll take it.

00:15:52.593 --> 00:15:54.549
Okay, Murdolator's finished.

00:15:57.640 --> 00:16:01.474
I said I'd kill him myself,
but nobody listens to Bender.

00:16:01.561 --> 00:16:03.517
We all have to
share in the guilt,

00:16:03.604 --> 00:16:07.267
which is why we're each going to add
one drop of cyanide to the death wheel

00:16:07.358 --> 00:16:08.393
as it goes by.

00:16:19.745 --> 00:16:24.034
Commence mercy-killing
in three, two, a-yup.

00:16:26.711 --> 00:16:27.996
Kill-check one is go.

00:16:45.563 --> 00:16:46.552
Kill-check two is go.

00:17:01.579 --> 00:17:03.035
Ooh!

00:17:04.123 --> 00:17:05.704
Lt's about time.

00:17:13.591 --> 00:17:15.331
Vegetables activated.

00:17:24.185 --> 00:17:25.516
Kill-check three is go.

00:17:25.603 --> 00:17:27.309
Also, the salad's ready.

00:17:27.438 --> 00:17:29.099
Yes!
Salad!

00:17:29.190 --> 00:17:30.521
What the hell are you doing?

00:17:32.109 --> 00:17:34.976
Zoidberg, we know about
your secret agreement.

00:17:35.071 --> 00:17:37.813
I am so, so sorry
for how we treated you.

00:17:37.907 --> 00:17:40.649
And to make it up to you, we're
killing the Professor for you

00:17:40.743 --> 00:17:43.155
so he doesn't die horribly
from hyper-malaria.

00:17:43.245 --> 00:17:46.328
He doesn't have hyper-malaria,
you idiots.

00:17:48.584 --> 00:17:50.120
He has Yeti-ism.

00:17:51.587 --> 00:17:53.703
When he saved my life
all those years ago,

00:17:53.798 --> 00:17:55.413
he was scratched
by a Yeti.

00:17:57.718 --> 00:18:01.802
Hmm. I consider myself almost
completely ignorant of modern medicine,

00:18:01.889 --> 00:18:03.470
and I've never
heard of Yeti-ism.

00:18:03.557 --> 00:18:06.924
It mimics the symptoms
of hyper-malaria exactly

00:18:07.019 --> 00:18:10.887
except for the part where instead
of dying, you turn into a Yeti.

00:18:11.148 --> 00:18:12.433
Ah!

00:18:18.072 --> 00:18:21.781
Wow. Hold him down while
I prepare the antidote.

00:18:25.329 --> 00:18:26.364
Another Yeti?

00:18:26.455 --> 00:18:30.494
Yes, the same jerk that once
noshed on me like a shrimp toast.

00:18:30.584 --> 00:18:34.247
Now who's getting
his pineal gland extracted?

00:18:36.507 --> 00:18:40.796
Yes, this contains a concentrated
form of the Yeti neurotoxin.

00:18:41.137 --> 00:18:43.674
But that's what gave him
Yeti-ism in the first place.

00:18:43.764 --> 00:18:45.220
Won't it just make him
a double-Yeti?

00:18:45.307 --> 00:18:48.299
Don't lecture me about
allen physiology, Conrad.

00:18:48.394 --> 00:18:52.057
The pineal neurotoxin neutralizes
the adrenal neurotoxin.

00:18:52.148 --> 00:18:54.309
That's why Yetis don't
drive themselves mad.

00:18:59.530 --> 00:19:02.738
My God, he's like some kind
of believable Hulk.

00:19:02.825 --> 00:19:05.191
No time for an injection.

00:19:15.629 --> 00:19:16.835
Ah!

00:19:22.928 --> 00:19:26.170
I'll be damned.
It did make him a double-Yeti.

00:19:55.586 --> 00:19:59.124
Lt wasn't supposed to do
any of those things.

00:20:07.515 --> 00:20:10.552
You did it, Johnny.
I'm cured!

00:20:19.068 --> 00:20:21.480
All right, let's set
it up and try again.

00:20:25.866 --> 00:20:28.528
There's one thing
I don't understand, Zoidberg.

00:20:28.619 --> 00:20:32.407
How did you persuade Mom to
give you her precious Yeti head?

00:20:32.498 --> 00:20:34.910
Did you have to
promise anything in return?

00:20:35.793 --> 00:20:38.535
Nothing, nothing at all.

00:20:38.629 --> 00:20:43.498
This calls for a celebration. Come
on, everyone, let's go tanning.

00:20:43.592 --> 00:20:45.753
Hurray!

00:20:48.430 --> 00:20:51.593
I was going to tan once.

00:20:52.768 --> 00:20:55.475
What do you say, Johnny?
Lt's on me.

00:20:57.022 --> 00:20:58.762
Thank you, Hubert.